<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#carolingian-minuscule">Glossary</a> · Term · script</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carolingian minuscule</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carolingian minuscule is a clear, legible script developed in the late eighth century in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a>. It was used to copy classical and religious texts in monastic scriptoria during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-renaissance">Carolingian Renaissance</a>. Revived by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> humanists, it became the basis of modern lower-case letters.</p></div>
